{"authored" [{"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/66bf8c1144de1ad65938345d2937fddd6fb43ec4822a2b98a9b5383ca2609567.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/97cf633bce7a8eeef443757e62d52f356c911b6aee3d8019d434d514416b0049.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\pi $ and $x=0$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi }^{0} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3})-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dbdad623d43671805a1cf25e54c1bfbc603831b9e5635a2c304f874410921eeb" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/state.json" "file_sha256" "67622c4c671e19b310b5301aa2814017636df559bb1eab68741ac932a7957da3" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/example-781.json" "file_sha256" "c9a9c600744b415fd48bc7ef3b773aca59f4e42bd56ff68e9f6dd91f9fb8cab0" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/example-781.json" "file_sha256" "c9a9c600744b415fd48bc7ef3b773aca59f4e42bd56ff68e9f6dd91f9fb8cab0" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/example-782.json" "file_sha256" "276ce04d087c93e79aa2a23f6efa7f9ec928dfe9351aa289342eb9e566f444ce" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/example-782.json" "file_sha256" "276ce04d087c93e79aa2a23f6efa7f9ec928dfe9351aa289342eb9e566f444ce" "basis" 1102 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-345321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/2102626f331aaa7803462f8e427ef2c0150deb554955199f3d402123934e815a.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-1$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{12}-(-\\frac{25}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d152ab99adebc94a5b39667c0ceb80422e36ff776e0d5cc19bbdec1fcbd326c4"} {"question" "q-345321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{14}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-11020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/36a6f536866d34703f0900304a5859518461fdf0d8c1df42e5269a253c9c3ff2.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=2$, shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-11020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+7{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{1}^{2}+7\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{1}^{2}-2\\cdot x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{(2)^{4}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4})+7(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})-2(2-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{2}+\\frac{49}{3}-2 \\\\  & =\\frac{41}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-11020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d152ab99adebc94a5b39667c0ceb80422e36ff776e0d5cc19bbdec1fcbd326c4"} {"question" "q-11020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-11020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{20}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{64}"] ["math" "\\frac{41}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{83}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{91}{20}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-11020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{41}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/ee37408e644416b0fe2d127703e6c5b531ae469e92d4119436fbb7f2b93ef573.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){|}_{1}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d152ab99adebc94a5b39667c0ceb80422e36ff776e0d5cc19bbdec1fcbd326c4"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡1"] ["math" "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡2"] ["math" "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1"] ["math" "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d152ab99adebc94a5b39667c0ceb80422e36ff776e0d5cc19bbdec1fcbd326c4"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/66bf8c1144de1ad65938345d2937fddd6fb43ec4822a2b98a9b5383ca2609567.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d152ab99adebc94a5b39667c0ceb80422e36ff776e0d5cc19bbdec1fcbd326c4"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-73324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/333a99cd7b1f4aa0c3017c2b5aa42cb04acad842b19345a1176d57a71c5fd120.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-{sec}^{2}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Find the area of the region." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-73324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-73324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d152ab99adebc94a5b39667c0ceb80422e36ff776e0d5cc19bbdec1fcbd326c4"} {"question" "q-73324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-73324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "1.4"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2.8"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-73324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3})-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d152ab99adebc94a5b39667c0ceb80422e36ff776e0d5cc19bbdec1fcbd326c4"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-345343" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/d07ef9eb8b578cd9f5f0c2c57caa44760b0a5e21d95bb0961fcff722276a7b4e.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y={x}^{2}-4$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=-2$ and $x=2$, shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{2}-4x{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})-4(2+2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{32}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d152ab99adebc94a5b39667c0ceb80422e36ff776e0d5cc19bbdec1fcbd326c4"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9244a4c62c14ea73269464aa0d2fa05b329c4466defaa0da10d53a54b4d28b2"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] [